repository-code: 'https://github.com/zackska/cfd-optical-diagnostics'
abstract: >-
  Two complementary ray tracers for predicting what a camera would
  record looking through a CFD field, plus the detector emulation
  needed to make a synthetic image comparable to a measurement. A
  CUDA renderer (gpuShadow) marches rays through a sampled volume and
  produces shadowgraph transmittance, deflection fields, classical
  schlieren and background-oriented schlieren displacement; a VTK/C++
  tracer handles triangulated surfaces. The BOS path additionally
  emulates a real rig - printed target, optical PSF, shot and read
  noise, quantisation, windowed FFT cross-correlation with
  loss-of-pairs correction - because the ground-truth displacement
  field is not directly measurable in an experiment.
keywords:
  - shadowgraphy
  - schlieren
  - background-oriented schlieren
  - synthetic diagnostics
  - ray tracing
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - atomization
  - OpenFOAM
  - CUDA
